 ## Feature gates
 
-The Automations gate is **fire-only**: telemetry continues updating its snapshots and a paused signal is treated as consumed, so an unchanged snapshot does not run after End. It blocks automatic and explicit runs, including action groups called from keys and quick controls, while leaving saved definitions intact. The Key Mapping gate rejects physical-key action dispatch while leaving stored bindings intact. Ending Service Mode reopens the gates.
+The Automations gate is **fire-only**: telemetry continues updating its snapshots and a paused signal is treated as consumed, so an unchanged snapshot does not run after End. It blocks automatic and explicit runs, including action groups called from keys and quick controls, while leaving saved definitions intact. The Key Mapping gate rejects physical-key action dispatch while leaving stored bindings intact.
+
+The **Proximity** gate rejects phone and keyfob observation-driven lock/unlock actions, including the final actuation/confirmation checks, while retaining trusted devices and user configuration. It does not disable the separate radar-based Proximity Guard recording mode.
+
+The **RoadSense** gate reconciles its running controller to the disabled state (releasing its detector, sensor sidecar and warning worker) while leaving `roadSense.enabled` unchanged. When the visit ends it reconciles back to the saved configuration.
+
+The **Widgets** gate stops the on-screen Glass Widgets overlay in the app process and prevents boot/keepalive and manual Arrange from restarting it. It does not delete layouts or widgets. The app-side service checks the persisted state independently of the daemon.
+
+The **Seat Positions** gate rejects POST changes and applies at `/api/positions` and suppresses accessibility-initiated captures, but keeps read-only listing and live status available. It does not touch the head unit's native BYD seat-memory controls.
+
+Ending Service Mode reopens all gates. The paused choices also take effect after a reboot because their state is persisted.
 
